[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Modern Cavemen]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.20]Lesson 42 | 第42课
[00:02.20]Modern cavemen | 现代洞穴人
[00:09.46]With what does the writer compare the Gouffre Berger? | 作者把高弗·伯杰洞比作什么？
[00:15.31]Cave exploration, or pot-holing, as it has come to be known, is a relatively new sport. | 洞穴勘察——或洞穴勘探，正如它已为人所知的那样——是一项较新的运动。
[00:23.34]Perhaps it is the desire for solitude or the chance of making an unexpected discovery that lures people down to the depths of the earth. | 也许是寻求独处或渴望有意外的发现，诱使人们来到地球深处。
[00:34.42]It is impossible to give a satisfactory explanation for a pot-holer's motives. | 要给洞穴勘探者的动机作出令人满意的解释是不可能的。
[00:40.92]For him, caves have the same peculiar fascination which high mountains have for the climber. | 对洞穴勘探者来说，洞穴对登山者所具有的那种特殊的魅力。
[00:48.99]They arouse instincts which can only be dimly understood. | 它们唤起的本能只能被模糊地理解。
[00:54.42]Exploring really deep caves is not a task for the Sunday afternoon rambler. | 勘探真正深的洞穴不是周日午后漫步者的任务。
[01:00.19]Such undertakings require the precise planning and foresight of military operations. | 这类行动需要军事行动般的周密部署和远见。
[01:08.04]It can take as long as eight days to rig up rope ladders and to establish supply bases before a descent can be made into a very deep cave. | 在能下到一个很深的洞穴之前，光搭建绳梯和建立供应基地就可能需要多达8天时间。
[01:20.61]Precautions of this sort are necessary, for it is impossible to foretell the exact nature of the difficulties which will confront the pot-holer. | 这类预防措施是必要的，因为无法预见洞穴勘探者将会遇到的困难的确切性质。
[01:32.06]The deepest known cave in the world is the Gouffre Berger near Grenoble. | 世界上最深的已知洞穴是格勒诺布尔附近的高弗·伯杰洞。
[01:38.66]It extends to a depth of 3, 723 feet. | 它深达3723英尺。
[01:44.33]This immense chasm has been formed by an underground stream which has tunnelled a course through a flaw in the rocks. | 这个巨大的洞穴是由一条地下溪流穿透岩石裂隙冲蚀而成的。
[01:53.65]The entrance to the cave is on a plateau in the Dauphine Alps. | 洞穴的入口在多芬阿尔卑斯山的高原上。
[02:00.13]As it is only six feet across, it is barely noticeable. | 由于入口只有6英尺宽，很不显眼。
[02:05.39]The cave might never have been discovered had not the entrance been spotted by the distinguished French pot-holer, Berger. | 若不是法国著名洞穴勘探家伯杰发现了这个入口，这个洞穴也许永远不为人知。
[02:15.00]Since its discovery, it has become a sort of pot-holers' Everest. | 自被发现以来，它已成为洞穴勘探者们的某种“珠穆朗玛峰”。
[02:20.66]Though a number of descents have been made, much of it still remains to be explored. | 虽然已多次有人下洞，但大部分洞穴尚待勘探。
[02:27.85]A team of pot-holers recently went down the Gouffre Berger. | 最近，一队洞穴勘探者下到了高弗·伯杰洞。
[02:33.27]After entering the narrow gap on the plateau, | 从高原上的狭窄裂口进入之后，
[02:36.96]they climbed down the steep sides of the cave until they came to a narrow corridor. | 他们沿着陡峭的洞壁向下爬，来到一条狭窄的走廊。
[02:43.62]They had to edge their way along this, | 他们不得不侧着身子挤过去，
[02:46.29]sometimes wading across shallow streams, or swimming across deep pools. | 有时蹚过浅溪，有时游过深潭。
[02:52.62]Suddenly they came to a waterfall which dropped into an underground lake at the bottom of the cave. | 突然，他们来到一个瀑布前，瀑布泻入洞底的一个地下湖中。
[03:00.69]They plunged into the lake, and after loading their gear on an inflatable rubber dinghy, let the current carry them to the other side. | 他们跳入湖中，把装备装上充气橡皮筏之后，让水流把他们带到对岸。
[03:11.67]To protect themselves from the icy water, they had to wear special rubber suits. | 为了抵御冰冷的水，他们不得不穿上特制的橡胶服。
[03:18.58]At the far end of the lake, they came to huge piles of rubble which had been washed up by the water. | 在湖的尽头，他们遇到了被水冲上来的大堆碎石。
[03:26.87]In this part of the cave, they could hear an insistent booming sound | 在洞穴的这一地段，他们能听到一种持续不断的轰鸣声，
[03:32.17]which they found was caused by a small waterspout shooting down into a pool from the roof of the cave. | 后来发现这是从洞顶射入水潭的小水柱造成的。
[03:40.42]Squeezing through a cleft in the rocks, the pot-holers arrived at an enormous cavern, the size of a huge concert hall. | 挤过岩石中的一道裂缝，洞穴勘探者来到一个巨大的洞窟，其规模像一座音乐厅。
[03:49.72]After switching on powerful arc lights, | 打开高功率弧光灯之后，
[03:53.00]they saw great stalagmites--some of them over forty feet high--rising up like tree-trunks to meet the stalactites suspended from the roof. | 他们看到巨大的石笋——有些高达40多英尺——像树干一样拔地而起，与洞顶悬垂下来的钟乳石相接。
[04:05.43]Round about, piles of limestone glistened in all the colours of the rainbow. | 四周成堆的石灰石闪烁着彩虹般的各种颜色。
[04:12.14]In the eerie silence of the cavern, the only sound that could be heard was made by water which dripped continuously from the high dome above them. | 在洞窟怪异的寂静中，唯一能听到的声音是水珠从他们上方高高的圆顶不断滴落的声音。
